# Lesson 3, new exercise: a partscore with six losers; dummy ruffs the third diamond.
title: Six losers in 2♥
id: L03-11
type: exercise
lesson: 3
concepts: 3.3
student: S
board: 43
dealer: S
vulnerable: none

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  K842   T652   92     Q53
  E  75     73     QJT3   AKJT9
  S  A63    AKQJ4  864    72
  W  QJT9   98     AK75   864

auction:
  S 1H*    = 13+ points, at least four hearts
     not *: 14 high-card points and five hearts: what does the lesson open?
  W Pass
  N 2H     = 6-9 points and heart support
  E Pass
  S Pass*  = No game: at most 24
     key: 15 points with the doubleton. Partner has at most 9, so your side has at most 24. Pass.
     not *: Did you add it up? 15 plus 9 is only 24.
  W Pass

auction recap:
  You opened 1♥ and partner raised to 2♥, showing 6-9 points. Your side
  can't have 25, so you stopped in a partscore. You are declarer, because
  you bid hearts first, and so West will lead to the first trick.

planning:
  trumps out: 4
  losers: 5
  spades: 1 = The third spade.
  hearts: 0 = Solid.
  diamonds: 2 = Three small ones, but dummy can ruff the third.
  clubs: 2 = The ace and king.
  remind: In 2♥ you need 8 tricks, so you can afford five losers. Count the obvious losers suit by suit in your own hand.
  remind: Dummy has only two diamonds. What can it do on the third round?
play:
  1   W DA  N D2  E D3  S D4
      note: Six losers: one spade, three diamonds and two clubs. One too many. But dummy has only two diamonds, so it can ruff your third one.
  2   W DK  N D9  E DT  S D6
  3   W H9  N H2  E H3  S HJ
      note: West sees that dummy is out of diamonds and leads a trump, hoping to stop the ruff.
  4   S D8  W D5  N H5  E DJ
      note: Ruff your last diamond loser in dummy now, before the opponents can lead another trump.
      ok: H
  5   N H6  E H7  S HQ  W H8
      note: Now draw the opponents' last trumps.
  6   S SA  W S9  N S2  E S5
      note: The spades: ace and king, then the loser you counted.
  7   S S3  W ST  N SK  E S7
      note: Then the ♠K.
  8   N S4  E C9  S S6  W SJ
      note: Your third spade is a loser. Give it up.
  9   W C8  N C3  E CJ  S C2
  10  E CA  S C7  W C6  N C5
  11  E CK  S H4  W C4  N CQ
  12  S HA  W SQ  N HT  E DQ
      note: Your last two trumps take the last two tricks.
  13  S HK  W D7  N S8  E CT
      note: 8 tricks: 2♥ made.

play recap:
  The plan: count six losers, one more than 2♥ can afford, and ruff the
  third diamond in dummy.

  West tried to stop the ruff by leading a trump, but dummy still had
  enough trumps left to take care of the third diamond.
